<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nguyễn Trãi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1380">1380</a>–<a href="/years/1442">1442</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Nguyen Trai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nguyễn Trãi was a Vietnamese scholar, poet and strategist who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-loi">Lê Lợi</a>'s chief adviser in the war against Ming occupation. He wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binh-ngo-dai-cao">Bình Ngô đại cáo</a>, the proclamation of victory of 1428, and poetry in both classical Chinese and vernacular Nôm. Accused in the sudden death of the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-thai-tong">Lê Thái Tông</a>, he was executed with his family in 1442 and later exonerated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nguyen-trai.jpg" alt="Nguyễn Trãi" width="320" height="476" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nguyen_Trai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
